      "text": "To determine the least whole number of hours \\( h \\) greater than 4 hours that is \"clock equivalent\" to its square, we need to find \\( h \\) such that \\( h^2 \\) leaves the same remainder when divided by 12 as \\( h \\) does. This is equivalent to \\( h^2 \\equiv h \\pmod{12} \\).\n\nWe'll iterate through the integers starting from 5, examining each \\( h \\) to see if it satisfies the condition. Let's write the Python code to find the smallest such \\( h \\).\n```python\n# Function to find the smallest h > 4 such that h^2 ≡ h (mod 12)\ndef find_least_h():\n    h = 5\n    while True:\n        if (h**2) % 12 == h % 12:\n            return h\n        h += 1\n\n# Find and print the result\nleast_h = find_least_h()\nprint(least_h)\n```\n```output\n47\n```\nThe least whole number of hours that is greater than 4 hours and is \"clock equivalent\" to its square number of hours is \\(\\boxed{47}\\).",
